{"availability":"available","full":"WordPress/contributor-toolkit","name":"contributor-toolkit","description":"Desktop app that sets up a WordPress core development environment with no prerequisites, applies the work already on a Trac ticket, and submits a contribution back.","category":"Developer tools","language":"JavaScript","stars":45,"forks":17,"created":"2025-10-01T14:30:09Z","updated":"2026-10-09T13:59:48Z","license":"GPL-2.0","branch":"trunk","homepage":"https://wordpress.github.io/contributor-toolkit/","topics":[],"demo":"https://wordpress.github.io/contributor-toolkit/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:41.112Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:41.112Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:41.112Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T16:43:41.112Z","stars":45,"forks":17}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The WordPress Contributor Toolkit is a desktop Electron application (macOS on Apple Silicon, Windows, and Linux) that takes a contributor from nothing to a working development environment for WordPress Core or Gutenberg, lets them try the work that already exists on a Trac ticket or a GitHub issue, and lets them send their own change back: as a pull request, a Trac attachment, or a patch for a mentor. No Git, Node.js, npm or Docker on the host, and no push credential written to disk.","One of the most common complaints from Contributor Day facilitators is this: participants spend the entire session trying to set up their local environment and never get to actually contribute.","Before writing a single line of code, a first-time WordPress core contributor typically needs to install Git, Node.js, npm, Docker, configure everything correctly, and troubleshoot whatever breaks along the way. At in-person events, this alone can take hours — sometimes the full day."],"features":["WordPress Core Dev Environment Toolkit: A Faster Path to Your First Core Contribution (April 2026)","WordPress Contributor Toolkit 1.0: A smoother workflow for your first Core contribution (August 2026)","WordPress Contributor Toolkit 1.2: One app for your first Core or Gutenberg contribution (September 2026)","Create a WordPress Core or Gutenberg development site with nothing installed on the host. A Core site is a wordpress-develop checkout; a Gutenberg site is a gutenberg checkout served as a plugin in a stock WordPress.…","Link a Trac ticket to a Core site and read its facts in the app: summary, status and resolution, type, milestone, component, keywords, age. A ticket can also arrive from a browser: the app answers wpct://ticket/62281…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/WordPress/contributor-toolkit/blob/trunk/README.md","fingerprint":"96d538b671d901c076e826794add32256e9e7f3aad8642e9fec65fbf7bb6b6c9","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:41.196Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:41.196Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"The WordPress Contributor Toolkit is a desktop Electron application (macOS on Apple Silicon, Windows, and Linux) that takes a contributor from nothing to a working development environment for WordPress Core or Gutenberg, lets them try the work that already exists on a Trac ticket or a GitHub issue, and lets them send their own change back: as a pull request, a Trac attachment, or a patch for a mentor. No Git, Node.js, npm or Docker on the host, and no push credential written to disk.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/WordPress/contributor-toolkit/blob/trunk/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Send the change back: a GitHub pull request to wordpress-develop or WordPress/gutenberg, opened through device sign-in with no credential on disk, a patch attached to Trac (Core only), or a patch handed to a mentor that keeps your name on the work.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/WordPress/contributor-toolkit/blob/trunk/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"96d538b671d901c076e826794add32256e9e7f3aad8642e9fec65fbf7b